.TH PY-TUNER 1 "" "py-tuner 0.3.0" "py-tuner"
.SH NAME
py\-tuner \- an accurate tuner for guitar, bass, double bass and violin
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B py\-tuner
[gui | tui | cli | devices | instruments] [\-a\ HZ] [\-i\ INSTRUMENT] [\-t\ TUNING] [\-f\ WAV] [...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
An accurate tuner for guitar, bass, double bass and violin (and a chromatic one), with a needle and a strobe, in a window, in the terminal or on the command line.

Without a command, the window opens. Options given here override the saved settings for this session only, unless \-\-save is given. Settings: ~/.config/py\-tuner/settings.json
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help and quit
.TP
.B \-\-version
show the version and quit
.TP
.B mode
gui (the window, default), tui (full\-screen terminal), cli (a line of text), tone (play a reference note), devices (list the inputs), instruments (list the tunings)
.TP
.B NOTE
tone: the note to play (e.g. E2), or a string number with \-\-instrument; A4 if none
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-a4
reference A4 in Hz, 380 to 480 (default 440)
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-instrument
the instrument, or chromatic (one of: chromatic, guitar, bass, double\-bass, violin)
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-tuning
the tuning, by name (e.g. "Drop D")
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-string
tune against string N (1 = the lowest) instead of the nearest one
.TP
.B \-\-names
note names: english, latin or german (one of: english, latin, german)
.TP
.B \-\-accidentals
write accidentals as sharps, flats or both (F#/Gb) (one of: sharps, flats, both)
.TP
.B \-\-flats
write accidentals as flats
.TP
.B \-\-sharps
write accidentals as sharps
.TP
.B \-\-tolerance
in tune within this many cents (default 1)
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-device
input device: its number or part of its name
.TP
.B \-r, \-\-rate
sample rate (default: the device's)
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-channel
use channel N (from 1) or the mix of all
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-file
read a WAV file instead of the sound card
.TP
.B \-\-min\-level
ignore sounds quieter than this (default \-60)
.TP
.B \-\-learn\-noise
also ignore what does not stand 10 dB over the room's noise, learned while nothing plays (the default)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-learn\-noise
only the fixed level of \-\-min\-level
.TP
.B \-\-smoothing
seconds the reading averages (default 0.5)
.TP
.B \-\-periods
periods per analysis frame: more is steadier, fewer is faster (default 16)
.TP
.B \-\-response
normal, or steady: the attack of each pluck left out, a longer average and a slower needle, for the double bass (default normal) (one of: normal, steady)
.TP
.B \-\-offset
tune a note name this many cents off equal temperament, in every octave (e.g. B=\-2; B=0 removes it); may be repeated
.TP
.B \-\-transpose
show the names transposed, for a transposing instrument (e.g. 2 for B\-flat)
.TP
.B \-\-capo
a capo at this fret raises every string
.TP
.B \-\-display
needle, strobe or both (gui, tui) (one of: both, needle, strobe)
.TP
.B \-\-strobe
the strobe: vernier (the clearest partial at three speeds) or harmonics (partials 1, 2 and 3) (one of: vernier, harmonics)
.TP
.B \-\-trace
show the history of the deviation (gui, tui)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-trace
hide the history of the deviation
.TP
.B \-\-spectrum
show the spectrum, with its peaks named (gui, tui)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-spectrum
hide the spectrum
.TP
.B \-\-needle
the needle's scale: linear, or fine (the centre spread out) (one of: linear, fine)
.TP
.B \-\-language
the language of the interface (default: the system's) (one of: en, es)
.TP
.B \-\-once
cli: print the first steady reading and exit
.TP
.B \-\-realtime
cli with \-\-file: play the file at its own pace instead of analysing it at once
.TP
.B \-\-save
save the options given as the new settings
.SH KEYS OF THE TERMINAL INTERFACE
.TP
.B q
Quit
.TP
.B ← / →
Lower / raise the reference A4 by 0.1 Hz
.TP
.B ↓ / ↑
Lower / raise the reference A4 by 1 Hz
.TP
.B 0
Put the reference A4 back to 440 Hz
.TP
.B i
The next instrument
.TP
.B t
The next tuning of the instrument
.TP
.B s
Lock the next string (after the last one, back to the nearest string)
.TP
.B n
The next system of note names: English, Latin, German
.TP
.B b
Sharps, flats or both
.TP
.B v
Needle and strobe, the needle alone or the strobe alone
.TP
.B m
The strobe: vernier (one partial, three speeds) or harmonics (partials 1, 2, 3)
.TP
.B h
Show or hide the history of the deviation
.TP
.B c
Move the capo one fret up (after the 7th, off)
.TP
.B f
Show or hide the spectrum, with its peaks named
.TP
.B g
The needle's scale: linear, or fine (the centre spread out)
.TP
.B r
The response: normal, or steady (for the double bass)
.TP
.B p
Play the reference tone: the locked string, or the note shown, or A4
.TP
.B l
The next language of the interface
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/py\-tuner/settings.json
The settings, the same for the window, the terminal and the command line ($XDG_CONFIG_HOME). Own tunings can be added in it, under custom_tunings.
